  data: {
    LLM: "Partnership Communication: Only the highest meld declaration at the table counts for that point category. Communicate with your partner to ensure your team's best meld is prioritized.\n\nThe 'Nine' Strategy: If your partner bids (takes), and you hold the Nine of trumps (Nell), try to lead it as early as possible if you suspect the opponent holds the Over-knave (Jass).\n\nDefensive Ducking: If your team is the defender, don't always trump in. Sometimes it's better to lose a trick to save a high card for the 'Last Trick' (10 points).",
